      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, this patch is required for the upcoming production release (I\u0027m not sure I can mention specific timelines here in AOSP) to provide the required security functionality (i.e. full DMA isolation for untrusted devices).\n\nAlso, as it turns out, we require this patch for performance reasons as well: b/498467166#comment114. At the moment the lack of this patch is blocking ODM validation of WiFi performance on official builds.\n\nWe can wait for upstream just a bit longer, but not much longer, I think.\n\nLet me also just quote my above comment:\n\nThis is the same patch that was merged into android16-6.12 last year in aosp/3507370. Also it was approved by Greg KH on LKML last year [1] but still didn\u0027t end up merged into the upstream kernel. I resent it to the list 3 weeks ago [2], now waiting for a response from maintainers. In the meantime we need this patch in GKI 6.18 to meet both security and performance requirements for untrusted DMA-capable devices on x86.\n\n[1] https://lore.kernel.org/all/2025022136-demanding-affluent-c72a@gregkh/\n[2] https://lore.kernel.org/all/20260525224023.2753569-1-dmaluka@chromium.org/",
